From 5f01c054832e97186bc4148bd5b95e2bb39715c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mozixun <ronforever@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:28:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] zink: don't charge a batch the whole slab for a suballocated
 resource

zink_bo_get_size() returns the slab a suballocation lives in, not the slice
the resource occupies, so moving N small resources into a batch charged N
slabs. For 1 KiB texture uploads that is ~2 MiB each, which reaches
clamp_video_mem and makes the batch end itself after a few thousand uploads
while almost nothing is actually live.

Charge the size the allocation owns instead. This only differs for
suballocated BOs; a dedicated allocation reports the same value either way.

Cc: mesa-stable
Generated-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: mozixun <ronforever@outlook.com>
